body:
Taking from: http://mustache.github.io/mustache.5.html it should be possible to pass variable into the helpers however, it is not quite working for me.

I have:

``` javascript
        instantsearch.widgets.hits({
            container: '#resultHolder',
            transformData: {
                item: function(o){
                    $.each(o.products, function(k, v){
                        o.products[k] = {idx: k, obj: v};
                    });
                    return o;
                }
            },
            templates: {
                empty: 'No results',
                item: '{{#products}}{{obj.id}}{{#helpers.button}}{{obj}}{{/helpers.button}}{{/products}}',
            },
            hitsPerPage: 20
        })
```

now `{{obj.id}}` works perfectly fine but `{{obj}}` just prints `{{obj}}` in this:

``` javascript
    search.templatesConfig.helpers.button = function(text){
        console.log(text);
    };
```

It seems that maybe there is something missing here?

comments.body:
Can you try using:

``` js
    search.templatesConfig.helpers.button = function(text){
        console.log(this); // this should be the entire item
    };
```

I am unsure objects are supported. Maybe also try:

``` js
    search.templatesConfig.helpers.button = function(text, render){
        console.log(render(text));
    };
```

